FBDD on several cores, with output identical to the serial code.

fbdd_correction and the first three passes of dcb_color_full only read values
they do not write; they get a parallel loop over rows. fbdd_green and the last
pass of dcb_color_full work in place and read already updated neighbours above
(and, for dcb_color_full, to the left); they run as a wavefront in which row i
computes a block of columns only after row i-1 has finished the next block.
The arithmetic is unchanged. Without LIBRAW_USE_OPENMP the code runs serially
in the original order.

Against LibRaw 40fb564486681a04eba0318058b0519f4f69eba8, apply with patch -p1.
The source file uses CRLF line endings; so do the changed lines.

